  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSI = Rs. 8,820\n\nRate = 6(3)/(4)% = 27/4%\n\nTime = 4(2)/(3) years = 14/3 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nSI = (P × R × T)/100\n\nA = SI + P\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nLet the sum is P\n\nSI = (P × R × T)/100\n\n⇒ 8820 = (P × 27 × 14)/(4 × 3 × 100)\n\n⇒ P = Rs. (140 × 200)\n\n⇒ P = Rs. 28,000\n\nNow,\n\nSI = (P × R × T)/100\n\n⇒ (28,000 × 25 × 15)/(3 × 2 × 100)\n\n⇒ Rs. (140 × 25 × 5)\n\n⇒ Rs. 17,500\n\nNow,\n\nAmount = SI + P\n\n⇒ Rs. (28,000 + 17,500)\n\n⇒ Rs. 45,500\n\n**∴ The required amount is Rs. 45,500**",
